sified_global coverage are relevant; no changed error source in this commit."},{"module":"Provider health store","owner":"v3/crates/routecodex-v3-provider-responses/src/health.rs; V3ProviderHealthStore::record_provider_failure_action owns streak, score, cooldown, and probe scheduling mutation","paths":"Unchanged consumer of the changed action fields","edges":"V3ProviderFailureRuntimeHealth::record_provider_key_failure_action -> V3ProviderHealthStore::record_provider_failure_action","resources":"Writes provider key health, failure streak, cooldown/probe state, and scheduling projection","gates":"Provider action gate, provider session cooldown, and global cooldown persistence gates apply; source tests alone do not establish live runtime evidence."}],"findings":[{"severity":"P1","file":"v3/crates/routecodex-v3-runtime/src/provider_failure_runtime_policy.rs","line":809,"rule":"post-commit SSE provider failures must preserve the existing transient-to-health-counted path","evidence":"The commit removes the prior HealthNeutralTransient branch that delegated to record_post_commit_provider_stream_failure (which constructs V3ProviderFailureAction::recoverable). For a source classified as HealthNeutralTransient, the new code passes that action directly through apply_v3_internal_provider_failure_policy with status 0; the normalizer leaves recovery=HealthNeutralTransient and failure_threshold=0. V3ProviderHealthStore::record_provider_failure_action only increments failure_streak, score, attempts, and cooldown state for IrrecoverableGlobalCooldown or RecoverableCounted, so post-commit transient SSE failures still enter the action gate but no longer count against global provider-key health or trigger cooldown/probing. This regresses the pre-existing behavior and affects the post-commit source path used by the relay outcomes.","remediation":"Retain the transient branch or otherwise explicitly convert HealthNeutralTransient to the existing recoverable counted action before record_provider_failure_record_with_action; add a regression test through record_post_commit_provider_stream_failure_from_source that submits three transient post-commit failures and asserts global key cooldown/fresh-session unavailability."}]}
